 \, 6:30PM Discussion\nExperience a behind-the-curtain look as The Huntin
 gton Theatre Company prepares to present the first regional production of 
 Aaron Sorkin’s acclaimed adaptation of To Kill a Mockingbird. Artistic 
 Director and Director of the production\, Loretta Greco joins fellow membe
 rs of the production to explore the art and complexity of bringing Harper 
 Lee’s enduring classic to the stage\, revealing what audiences rarely s
 ee: the journey from script to stage\, the artistic decisions made along t
 he way\, and the collaboration required to bring a production of this scal
 e to life. Together\, they will consider the delicate balance between hon
 oring a story that has resonated for generations and embracing the creativ
 e freedom and fresh perspective that come with a new interpretation.\n\n*T
 his event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary li
 ght bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancella
 tions be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
